# Rust Core Standards

- Prefer clear, small modules and explicit types on public APIs.
- Use `Result<T, E>` for fallible operations; avoid `unwrap()`/`expect()` in non-test code.
- Keep functions focused; extract helpers when a function mixes parsing, IO, and business logic.
- Favor immutable data; use mutability only where needed.
- Add concise comments only for non-obvious logic.

# Completion Checklist

Before declaring work done:
- `cargo fmt --all`
- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
- `cargo check --all-targets --all-features`
- `cargo test --all-targets --all-features`
